  "section_notes": "The final text sets S2 at a 7% permanent limit with no sales stop and keeps per-model rates out of public publication, which protects Northwind's 6.2% Hearth 10 but sits outside the 5% safe range. S3 gives a 24-month new-unit deadline and a 6-year retrofit, the latter matching Northwind's red line. S5 keeps the 8-per-100k mandatory recall trigger with no transition, which would catch Halcyon's 9.9 flagship, while S4's 36-month suppression start favours Halcyon's cost position."
